$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure D for the preparation of
4-hydroxy-isoquinolones 6 (Schemes 4 &amp; 5): 1) In air, 3 (1.0 equiv),
(if solid) 5 (1.0 equiv), Pd2(dba)3 (1 mol %), Xantphos (3 mol %) and
Cs2CO3 (1.4 equiv) were weighed in a 5-10 mL microwave vial equipped with
a stir bar. The vial was sealed, evacuated and backfilled with N2 (x3).
Dioxane (volume for [3] = 0.5 M) (and 5 if liquid) was added by syringe.
The reaction was stirred at 100 °C for 18 h. Then, the reaction mixture
was filtered through a pad of Celite (rinsed with CH2Cl2) and the
resulting filtrate was evaporated to afford 7, which was used without any
further purification. 2) The previous residue was solubilised in acetone
(same amount as dioxane) in a 2-5 mL microwave vial equipped with a stir
bar. 0.2 M aq Oxone (1.0 equiv) was added and the tube was sealed. The
reaction was vigorously stirred at rt for 2 h. Then, the reaction mixture
was poured into 1 M aq HCl and the resulting soln was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (x3). The combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4) and
evaporated to afford the crude product, which was purified by flash
chromatograph (eluted with mixtures of EtOAc and heptane) to afford 6. .
4-hydroxy-2-(4-trifluoromethylphenyl)-3,4-dihydroisoquinolin-1(2H)-one
6aa: Following general procedure D, the reaction performed with 3a (200
mg, 0.44 mmol) and 4-bromobenzotrifluoride 5a (61 uL, 0.44 mmol) afforded
6aa. .
4-hydroxy-2-(4-trifluoromethyl-3-pyridinyl)-3,4-dihydroisoquinolin-1(2H)-one
6af: Following general procedure D, the reaction performed with 3a (200
mg, 0.44 mmol) and 5-bromo-2-trifluoromethylpyridine 5f (99 mg, 0.44
mmol) afforded 6af. (107 mg, 79%) as a white solid. 1H NMR (400
MHz/acetone-d6): δ 8.95 (d, J= 2 Hz, 1H), 8.15 (dd, J= 8, 2 Hz, 1H), 8.07
(dd, J= 8, 1 Hz, 1H), 7.91 (d, J= 8 Hz, 1H), 7.67-7.59 (m, 2H), 7.50
(ddd, J= 8, 8, 2 Hz, 1H), 5.12-5.09 (m, 2H); 4.34-4.30 (m, 1H), 4.16-4.12
(m, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz/acetone-d6): δ 164.1 (C), 147.9 (CH), 144.4 (q,
J= 34 Hz, C), 143.5 (C), 142.3 (C), 134.0 (CH), 133.7 (CH), 129.3 (CH),
129.2 (CH), 128.9 (C), 127.5 (CH), 122.9 (q, J= 273 Hz, C), 121.4 (q, J=
2 Hz, C), 65.7 (CH), 56.2 (CH2). 19F NMR (377 MHz/acetone-d6): δ -67.9
(br). HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C15H12F3N2O2 (M + H)+ 309.0851, found
309.0833.
