$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure (A) for 1-Substituted
Imidazo[1,5-a]pyridines Reaction conditions were used according to the
previous literature.7 In the glove box, a vial (20 mL) was charged with
Pd(dba)2 (58 mg, 5 mol %), PtBu3 (41 mg,10 mol %), KOH (258 mg, 2.0
equiv), 1a-Br (394 mg, 2.0 mmol), and boronic acid (1.1 equiv) in dry DMF
(8 mL). After stirring for 5 minutes, the vial was screw-capped and taken
outside the glove box. Following 12 h of heating at 80 °C, the reaction
was cooled down to room temperature. The resulting residue was added
water and extracted with ethyl acetate. The combined organic layers were
dried with MgSO4, filtered through Celite, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by flash chromatography (EtOAc/hexane
= 1:1) on silica gel to afford pure products 1.
1-(Thiophen-2-yl)imidazo[1,5-a]pyridine (1m) The reaction was performed
according to the above general procedure (A) and 1m was obtained in 79%
yield as chartreuse solid. 1H NMR(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.06 (s, 1H), 7.84
(d, 3JHH = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 7.72 (d, 3JHH = 9.3 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (dd, 3JHH =
3.5, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.24-7.21 (m,1H), 7.09 (dd, 3JHH = 5.2, 3.6 Hz, 1H),
6.75 (dd, 3JHH = 9.4, 6.3 Hz,1H), 6.53 (t, 3JHH = 6.8 Hz, 1H). 13C{1H}
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 137.9, 127.2,126.7, 125.8, 125.0, 122.4, 122.0,
120.9, 119.8, 117.7, 112.4. HRMS (EI) m/z Calcd for C11H8N2S [M]+:
200.0408, Found: 200.0410.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Controlled Regiodivergent C-H Bond Activation of Imidazo[1,5-a]pyridine
via Synergistic Cooperation between Aluminum and Nickel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
