$DATUM 4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-(5-(3-bromothiophen)thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(7)
4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-(5-(trimethylstannyl)thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(374 mg, 1.00 mmol), [Pd(PPh3)4] (23 mg, 2 mol%,) and the
3-bromo-2-iodothiophene (289 mg, 1.00 mmol) was dissolved in DMF (4 mL).
The mixture was heated to 100 °C in a microwave apparatus for 120 min and
was then filtered over a short plug of celite. The solvent was removed in
vacuo and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
(n-hexanes/ethyl acetate (9:1). The product as a pale green solid in a
yield of 291 mg (79 %). Rf = 0.28; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.58 (d,
1H, 3 J = 3.7 Hz, Tph-H-c), 7.49 (d, 1H, 3 J = 3.7 Hz, Tph-H-b), 7.20 (d,
1H, 3 J = 5.4 Hz, Tph-H-g), 7.02 (d, 1H, 3 J = 5.4 Hz, Tph-H-h), 1.35 (s,
12H, pin-C(CH 3)4) ppm. 13C NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 141.1 (Tph-C-e),
137.2 (Tph-C-c), 132.3 (Tph-C-d), 132.1 (Tph-C-h), 127.8 (Tph-C-b), 124.8
(Tph-C-g), 108.5 (Tph-C-f), 84.3 (pin-C(CH3)4), 24.8 (pin-C(CH3)4) ppm.3
11B NMR (160 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 28.8 ppm. M.p.: 72 °C. IR (ATR): ν = 2974
(m), 2929(w), 1506 (m), 1458 (s), 1325 (s), 1268 (s), 1212 (w), 1138 (s),
1065 (s), 1015 (m), 957 (w), 851 (s), 822 (s), 409 (s), 663 (s), 614 (m)
cm-1. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 372/370 (100)/(88) [M]+. MS (CI,
isobutane): m/z (%) =429/427 (24)/(17) [M + isobutane]+, 373/371
(100)/(99) [M + H]+. HRMS (ESI): m/z found 370.9949; calcd. for
C14H17BBrO2S2 370.9941.
