$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Suzuki Procedure (GP 1): To an oven
dried 2-neck flask (15 mL) equipped with a stir bar (Ar) was added SM (1
eq), ArB(OH)2 (1.1 eq), and Cs2CO3 (1.1 eq). A condenser was attached and
PhMe (N2 sparged), EtOH, and H2O (5.08:1:1.54, 0.025 M) were added. The
reaction was degassed using three cycles of the freeze, pump, thaw
method. Tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (0.07 eq) was then added
and the biphasic mixture heated to reflux (105 °C) and stirred vigorously
for 24 h. Prior to cooling the reaction was a biphasic translucent yellow
mixture. Upon cooling to rt the organic layer would turn black. This
reaction was partitioned between CH2Cl2 (5 mL) and H2O (5 mL). The layers
were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 25
mL). The combined organic layers were dried with MgSO4, filtered through
a cotton plug, and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash
chromatography with silica gel gave the desired product. From 11 (33.12
mg, 0.060 mmol), pyridine boronic acid (8.15 mg, 0.066 mmol), and Cs2CO3
(21.60 mg, 0.066 mmol). Next PhMe, EtOH, and H2O were added (1.59 mL:0.31
mL:0.48 mL, 0.025M) followed by tetrakis(triphenylphosphine) palladium
(4.88 mg, 0.0042 mmol). Purification by flash chromatography
(Et3N:MeOH:CH2Cl2, 1:4:95).
(R)-(2-(pyridin-4-yl)quinolin-4-yl)((S)-1-tritylpyrrolidin-2-yl)methanol
as a white foam, yield 25.62 mg, 78%. 1H NMR (500 MHz; CDCl3): δ 8.78 (d,
J = 5.8 Hz, 2H), 8.17-8.11 (m, 4H), 7.67-7.66 (m, 7H), 7.35 (t, J = 7.6
Hz, 6H), 7.29-7.26 (m, 3H), 7.23-7.20 (m, 1H), 6.42 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H),
5.85 (d, J = 2.9 Hz, 1H), 4.14-4.10 (m, 1H), 3.76 (br s, 1H), 3.36-3.31
(m, 1H), 3.17-3.13 (m, 1H), 1.82 (br s, 1H), 1.55-1.48 (m, 1H), 0.75-0.68
(m, 1H), 0.02-(-0.07) (m, 1H). 13C NMR (126 MHz; CDCl3): δ 154.3, 150.5,
148.7, 147.1, 144.3, 130.8, 130.2, 129.4, 128.6, 128.0, 126.9, 126.8,
125.2, 122.58, 121.9, 115.2, 78.3, 72.6, 64.5, 54.0, 26.1, 24.9. [α]25D:
-74.06 (c 0.061, CHCl3). HRMS (ESI): Molecular ion was not observed
because of ion suppression by trityl. UV: (CHCl3) λmax (log ε) 253 nm
(4.39).
